{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["The sense of <b>and from the wilderness, a gift</b> is according to the words of Onkelos (Onkelos on Numbers 21:18), and it is concise language as is fitting in songs. It says that from the wilderness — which is a land of dryness and thirst — this was a gift to us, and from the gift to the streams, and from the streams to the heights, as far as the Pisgah that looks out over the face of the land, which is entirely a howling waste, in which there is no other stream and no flowing spring besides this one. And it is the well of Miriam according to the opinion of our Sages (Numbers Rabbah 19:25–26), or a well that came forth at the word of Moses from the mouth of the Almighty, which Israel did not request, and HaShem said to him, \"Gather the people and I will give them water\" (Numbers 21:16), and streams would flow from it and run to distant places."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {0 "The verse quoted near the end, אסוף את העם ואתנה להם מים, is from Numbers 21:16, slightly paraphrased from the biblical text; rendered here as Ramban cites it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:26.570890033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}